{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.KnotFactorSpectralDerivation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.KnotFactorSpectralDerivation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.knotFactor_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.knotFactor_self","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L72-L87","doc":"**Self-pairing.**  Pairing a braid with itself gives the Plancherel\nsum of squared character ratios,\n\n  `a_K(β, β) = Σ_λ w_λ · (χ_λ(β) / χ_λ(𝟙))²` ,\n\nthe \"sum of positive squares\" form.  Over an ordered field every\nsummand with `w_λ ≥ 0` is non-negative, which is what makes the\namphicheiral corollary's sign flip on the alternating block\nobservable rather than a convention. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_spectral_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.knot_factor_spectral_form","kind":"theorem","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L55-L70","doc":"**Proposition (knot factor as chirality Gram pairing)**.\n\nFor any braid `β ∈ B_n` with mirror `β*`, the knot factor\nappearing in the unified mass formula is the Plancherel-weighted\ncharacter pairing displayed above. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:knot-factor-spectral-form","label":"prop:knot-factor-spectral-form","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/knot-factor-spectral-derivation.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.knotFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.knotFactor","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L49-L53","doc":"The knot-factor `a_K` as a Gram pairing on the chirality block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.trivial","kind":"def","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L47-L47","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.weight","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L46-L46","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.c","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L45-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.partitions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.partitions","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion.mk","kind":"ctor","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeExpansion","kind":"structure","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/5697c3130d79ead793a58c1a0a984a2e49b1365f/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/KnotFactorSpectralDerivation.lean#L40-L47","doc":"Central-idempotent character expansion of a braid in `H_n(q)`,\nover the Hecke base ring `R` (§7c: generic; `R := ℚ(q)` is the\nintended instance, `R := ℝ` the archimedean one). ","signatureChunk":0}]}